e old.","y":0.37132605974467214},{"w":0.29511277142693015,"h":0.010174418362704274,"t":"******************************","y":0.36337209305338625,"x":0.46992481360514404},{"t":"Verbal Sentences \/ Focuses and ma-Actor Focus","y":0.31818089325337096,"h":0.021800790266557124,"w":0.4777934713924632,"x":0.11070770847846823},{"y":0.29215116264136165,"t":"In the first four lessons you have learned how to make equational sentences. These","w":0.65413531135110303,"h":0.017441860545765242,"x":0.16729323840339602},{"x":0.11278195790232416,"w":0.23120300292968754,"h":0.013081394542347358,"t":"sentences do not have a verb.","y":0.2761627913189425},{"h":0.023767831975763487,"w":0.70897188074448514,"y":0.25322728404879735,"t":"In this lesson you will begin learning how to make Waray sentences which use a verb. We","x":0.16715590398682473},{"t":"call these verbal sentences. Verbal sentences, which contain a subject (an actor) and a verb, are","x":0.11090226501860195,"y":0.23818181785184955,"h":0.019090909090909158,"w":0.74624059340533089},{"t":"expanded by adding an object, a direction\/location, a beneficiary, or an instrument.","y":0.21897579429775138,"w":0.64876917221966912,"h":0.021450754512440051,"x":0.11074902548938713},{"h":0.020826046683571464,"x":0.16720738680845892,"y":0.18422624558937084,"w":0.67689173081341913,"t":"In Waray the TOPIC, or the emphasized part of the sentence, may be the subject, the"},{"x":0.11073510624368844,"y":0.16500814929988794,"t":"object, the direction\/location, the beneficiary, or the instrument. The emphasized part of the","w":0.72027465820312497,"h":0.02344576748934657},{"t":"sentence, or the topic, is marked by a I Class word. In English, words are emphasized by the","y":0.147646506257335,"h":0.023940864042802379,"x":0.11072444791709907,"w":0.7259268008961397},{"t":"raising of the voice or by prolonging the word. In Waray, however, words are given emphasis by","y":0.1292172558818524,"w":0.75979844037224264,"x":0.11070216377052475,"h":0.025011691180142459},{"w":0.74812026079963234,"t":"what is called VERB FOCUSES. There are several different verb forms, or focuses, in Waray.","y":0.11627907010444505,"h":0.018895348635586839,"x":0.11090228299304071}]}